# Build artifacts
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock is COMMITTED. This crate ships a binary artifact (an XCFramework
# built from an exact dependency set), so a reproducible build wins over the
# library convention of ignoring it.
# Do not add Cargo.lock here.

# The generated Swift is TRACKED, and the C half of it is not.
#
# `modelpipe_ffi.swift` is this package's Swift face: SwiftPM compiles it as a
# source target beside the binary one, so a consumer resolving a tag gets the
# binding and the `.a` as a matched pair. They have to be matched — the
# generated Swift carries UniFFI's API checksums and calls
# `fatalError("UniFFI API checksum mismatch")` when they disagree, which is a
# crash on a device at first dial rather than an error at build time.
#
# The header and modulemap are NOT tracked, because they are not read from
# here: `build-xcframework.sh` copies them into the XCFramework's Headers
# directory, which is where a consumer sees them.
#
# The comment this replaces said of the generated Swift and the framework that
# "both are attached to a release". Only the framework ever was. That false
# sentence is what hid the fact that nothing published the binding at all.
/generated/*FFI.h
/generated/*FFI.modulemap
/build
*.xcframework
*.xcframework.zip

# Secrets — nothing here should ever be a committed file, but this crate's
# whole subject is tickets and tokens, so make the mistake harder.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Local AI/assistant tooling — never tracked. Carried over from modelpipe and
# gglib, where these are scratch space for coding assistants (session state,
# worktrees, handoff notes). Machine-local, and must not enter history.
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
.continue/
.codeium/
.github/copilot-instructions.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# Editors / tooling
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.iml
.direnv/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Swift package build output from the consuming smoke test
.build/

# The spike's generated Xcode project. `make spike` regenerates it from
# spike/project.yml, which is the tracked source of truth — the same
# arrangement ggchat uses.
spike/*.xcodeproj
spike/Info.plist
